  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.36",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let a hierarchy of tdlc groups $\\mathbf H\\mathcal K$ be defined analogously to Kropholler's hierarchy in 15.45, with $\\mathcal K$ being the class of profinite groups and with the cell stabilisers of the admissible action required to be open. Is it true that $\\mathbf H\\mathcal K$ is closed under profinite extensions, that is, $(\\mathbf H_\\alpha\\mathcal K)\\mathcal K\\subseteq \\mathbf H_\\alpha\\mathcal K$ for every $\\alpha$?",
